# Climb2Cal

Welcome to climb2cal
This is a script i have written to sync my schedule from the reach with my google calender
its simple enough that there should'nt bee any issues on the script's end



***Using the app Locally***

run Climb2Cal.py, you will be prompted to enter your first and last name
(this will be saved and used to log into the reach's website, so use the same name as you do there)
then you will be prompted to connect your google account
you will get a warning that says the app has not been authenticated by google
this is expected, you can hit continue
and that's it, the script will add everything to a secondary calender in your google account 

the next time you run the program it will also make any changes (such as cancelled sessions, or start/end timings)
as well as adding any new sessions



***Home server automation***

if you happen to have access to a home server then i will be making a docker image soon.
i am happy to help you set it up once i have added it
that way you can automatically run the script at any time of day you choose, forever
this was the reason i made this whole thing in the first place

otherwise i have hosted the script on my own homeserver and it executes every day at 10pm automatically
and if i can figure out how to do so: ill be happy to run your script on my server too



##TROUBLESHOOTING##

-if you have entered your name incorrectly, please delete the 'login.json' file
-and if you wish to use a different google account please delete the "token.json" file
in both cases, run the script again :)

any issues just shoot me a message or find me at the reach, i'm more then happy to help
or email at pkaciemalone@gmail.com and reference 'Climb2Cal' somewhere :)


Enjoy! :3
